1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,927
This frog freezes solid every
winter, then comes back.

2
00:00:03,007 --> 00:00:05,422
Meet the wood frog, found
as far north as Alaska.

3
00:00:05,502 --> 00:00:07,545
When winter hits, ice
spreads through its body.

4
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:09,604
Up to sixty percent of it freezes solid.

5
00:00:09,684 --> 00:00:12,053
Then it stops breathing,
and its heart stops beating.

6
00:00:12,133 --> 00:00:14,284
It can stay like
this for as long as seven months.

7
00:00:14,364 --> 00:00:17,637
Its secret is sugar. The frog
floods its cells with glucose.

8
00:00:17,717 --> 00:00:21,252
That sugar lowers the freezing point
and protects its cells from ice.

9
00:00:21,332 --> 00:00:25,778
Alaskan wood frogs survive temperatures
as low as about ten degrees Fahrenheit.

10
00:00:25,858 --> 00:00:29,625
Then spring arrives, the frog thaws
out, and its heart starts beating again.

11
00:00:29,705 --> 00:00:32,494
Frozen for months, then
hopping again. Follow for more.

